/-- Option-valued admission decision (#140).  In `fxProfile`, every
generator is admitted, so this is always `some`.  Restricted profiles
would return `none` for unadmitted generators.

Returning `Option` rather than the bare witness gives downstream code a
uniform contract: `match supportedGeneratorV2? g with | some w => ... |
none => reject ...`.  For the current default profile, the `none` branch
is dead code but the interface is forward-compatible. -/
@[reducible] def supportedGeneratorV2? (generator : Generator) :
    Option (SupportedGeneratorV2 generator) :=
  some (supportedGeneratorV2 generator)

/-- The admission decision is always `some` under the default
`fxProfile` (all 194 generators admitted).  Proof: `rfl` after
unfolding — `supportedGeneratorV2?` is definitionally `some _`. -/
theorem supportedGeneratorV2?_isSome (generator : Generator) :
    (supportedGeneratorV2? generator).isSome = true := by
  rfl

